<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19414" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gĕnĕrābĭlis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		genero (postAug.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>that has the power of
				generating</i>, <i>generative</i>, <i>creative</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hic est ille generabilis rerum naturae
					spiritus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					2, 45, 45, § 116</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Pass.</i>, <i>that may be
			generated</i> or <i>produced</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opus generabile,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Manil. 1, 143</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>